Party Pack (working title)

Everything in this game is generated by its own code, except the font and
the engine's own files listed below:
  - tools/bake2d.mjs      the 2D art: lit sprites with normal maps (characters, props,
                          pads, gems, blocks, parallax ridges, clouds), decals
  - tools/make-textures.mjs  the PBR texture sets (steel, lava, wood, rock, sand, grass,
                          asphalt, kerb, felt, board tile, metal, velvet)
  - tools/make-models.mjs the 3D models as glb files (characters, arena, raft, buoys,
                          cliffs, track, karts, table, board tiles, trophy, podium)
  - tools/make-luts.mjs   the colour grades (.cube)
  - src/common.c          the sounds and music, synthesized at start-up
  - the scenes in assets/scenes/, the quiz questions in src/g_quiz.c
  - tools/blender/preview.py a CPU preview helper (Blender, not shipped)

Third-party files:
  - assets/fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf : Lilita One, by Juan Montoreano,
    SIL Open Font Licence 1.1 (assets/fonts/OFL-LilitaOne.txt).
    Source: https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/lilitaone
  - the engine's default fonts (Fira Sans / Fira Mono, SIL Open Font Licence
    1.1), see the engine's NOTICE.
  - cartwheel-engine, three.c, Box2D, Box3D and their dependencies: see the
    engine's NOTICE for each licence (MIT, zlib and BSD style licences).

No downloaded textures, models or images are used.

Design inspiration only (ideas such as a board with a ladder of rounds,
ready-up cards, CPUs filling empty seats; no code or assets taken): the
open source party game SuperTuxParty (GPL-3.0 code, CC-BY-4.0 assets).
